preConditionHook:
// THE "20 GAP BAR" PULLBACK BUY: the FIRST bar to touch the EMA after a run of
// gapBarsRequired bars that never touched it, closing back on the trend side.
// Brooks's claim is that buyers are waiting at the average after a run that
// long; the entry is what monetizes it.
//
// CARRIED WHOLE, and it is NOT EmaGapBarRun AND EmaTouch. The counter resets to
// 0 on the touch bar itself, so EmaGapBarRun evaluates FALSE on exactly the bar
// this rule fires. What this rule needs is the counter's PREVIOUS value, which
// no pair of ANDed panes can express -- the same argument that keeps every
// crossing rule whole. prevGap is captured at the top of the hook, BEFORE the
// update: locals persist across bars, so at that moment gapCount still holds
// the previous bar's streak. It is a plain local read and NOT the lagged
// function read XAverage(...)[k], which remains unmeasured.
//
// The touch tolerance in the sources (0 to 1 tick) is dropped in favour of the
// exact straddle test, as EmaTouch does, because MinMove/PriceScale give the
// engine no tick size. The limit-order mechanics of one source collapse under
// the standing signal-bar-close / next-bar-open convention.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls, MEASURED
// BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in AT A FIXED LENGTH ((wf - xa)
// exactly 0 on all 17,785 bars of EL_XAverage_Probe.txt, @OJ 240min): the SEED
// is the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar; the recurrence is ONE
// statement in EL's form, x + sf*(p - x), never sf*p + (1-sf)*x, because the
// two separate in floating point on 67% of bars past 100; there is NO WARM-UP
// HOLE, so no CurrentBar guard returning 0; an EMA never forgets its seed, so
// Max Bars Back and the chart start are part of the specification. UNMEASURED:
// the walkforward LENGTH CHANGE the wrapper exists for -- PIN emaLength in the
// grid until it is measured.
//
// emaSf is a localVariables entry rather than a hook-scope const so the hooks
// survive a double placement.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 0.
prevGap = gapCount;
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
touched = el_le(low[0], emaVal) && el_ge(high[0], emaVal);
if (touched) {
    gapCount = 0;
} else {
    gapCount = gapCount + 1;
}
